{
  "dom_id": "step-e12753",
  "name": "Example: Expressing a Plain English Sentence as a Formal Statement",
  "problem": "Express the following statement in formal language:\n\nThere is a prime $p$ that is even.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there is\" indicate we use an existential quantifier, $\\exists.$\n\n- The sentence refers to the prime numbers. So, by denoting a prime number as $p,$ we have that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14100660/assets/3680e42982fa38c96aac7e1c0730f8588c4d58ae4036332a255eadc27d60b676.png)\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as\n\n$$\np \\textrm{ is even.}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$\\exists$ $p$ prime, $p$ is even.\n\nWe could also write\n\n$\\exists$ $p$ prime, $2\\mid p.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
